content.text:
Confirmed — no horizontal padding anywhere in the `.pane`/`.tree-pane` chain, so the Feed panel's rows are edge-to-edge. Now I'll write up the full report.

## Report: Feed panel implementation

### File map (`apps/desktop/src/features/notes/navigation/`)

| Concern | File |
|---|---|
| Feed panel UI (top-level) | `ui/feed-panel.tsx` |
| Feed pseudo-folder grouping (by date) | `model/feed-tree-model.ts` (+ `model/feed-tree-model.test.ts`) |
| Shared recursive row renderer (folders **and** feed) | `ui/tree-node.tsx` |
| Shared "folder/bucket" row chrome (hover/selected/DnD) | `ui/tree-row.tsx` |
| Shared note row chrome | `ui/nav-note-row.tsx` |
| Feed-only keyboard nav (arrow keys) | `hooks/use-feed-keyboard-navigation.ts` |
| Folder-tree DnD engine (does **not** apply to Feed) | `hooks/use-drag-drop.ts`, `model/tree-dnd.ts`, `model/dnd-tree.ts` |
| Shared node/tree types | `model/types.ts` |
| Feed data plumbing (`feedTreeData`, `activeFeedGroup`, etc.) | `state/notes-tree-context.tsx`, `state/use-notes-tree-state.ts` |
| Real folder tree (contrast case) | `model/notes-tree-model.ts`, `ui/folders-panel.tsx`, `ui/sidebar-file-tree-node.tsx` |
| Generic click/select/toggle handlers used by the real Folders tree | `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/app/hooks/use-tree-interactions.ts` |
| Shift-click range-selection primitive | `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/shared/lib/selection.ts` |
| All the row CSS (this is a plain-CSS app for these rows, not Tailwind utilities) | `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/app/app.css` |
| shadcn Sidebar primitives (Tailwind, used only by the *real* Folders tree) | `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/shared/ui/sidebar.tsx` |
| Mount point / where Feed vs Folders tabs are wired | `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/desktop/desktop-app-shell.tsx` (lines 326-404), `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/desktop/app-sidebar.tsx` |

**Important structural fact:** the "Folders" tab in `desktop-app-shell.tsx` renders `<FoldersPanel ... embedded />` (line 401, `embedded` truthy), and `embedded=true` makes `FoldersPanel` render via `SidebarFileTreeNode` (`ui/sidebar-file-tree-node.tsx`), which uses the shadcn/Tailwind `SidebarMenuButton`/`SidebarMenuSubButton` primitives from `shared/ui/sidebar.tsx`. **Feed does not go through that path at all.** `FeedPanel` renders `TreeNode`/`TreeRow`/`NavNoteRow` directly (the same "plain" renderer `FoldersPanel` only uses when `embedded` is false, which the app currently never does for real folders). So today, Feed rows and Folders rows are built from two structurally different component trees, not just a `feedMode` flag on the same component — this is the root of any visual/font divergence.

---

### 1. Feed panel UI — `ui/feed-panel.tsx`

Full file read (241 lines). Key points:

- Line 1: `// Feed navigation renders synthetic time buckets, not the folder tree.`
- Pulls `feedTreeData`, `feedNodeById`, `activeFeedGroup`, `expanded`, `allNotePreviews`, `feedLoading`, `shouldNestNotesInNavigation` from `useNotesTree()` (context in `state/notes-tree-context.tsx`).
- `selectFeedGroup` (lines 64-91): clicking a bucket sets `activeFeedGroup`, forces `selectedFolders = {FEED_FOLDER_PATH}` (constant `"Feed"` from `@typenotes/shared/constants`), clears note selection, clears editor draft, and calls `focusNoScroll(paneBodyRef.current)`.
- `handleNoteSelect` (lines 93-126): computes multi-select range via `computeRangeSelection` (see §3 below) scoped to the notes of the note's *parent bucket* (`parentNode.notes.map(n => n.path)`), not the whole feed — i.e. shift-click range-selects only within the same date bucket.
- `handleToggle` (lines 128-142): expand/collapse a bucket, `event.stopPropagation()`.
- `handleNoteContextMenu` (lines 144-184): right-click handling, resolves `targetPaths` for multi-selection the same way as the shared `resolveTargetPaths` logic.
- Empty state (lines 186-192): `<div className="empty">{feedLoading ? "Loading feed..." : "No feed notes yet."}</div>`.
- Root render (lines 194-241):
```
<div className="nav-scroll-area" ref={paneBodyRef} tabIndex={0} onKeyDown={onPaneKeyDown} onClick={...}>
  <div className="pane-body tree-root feed-navigation-tree">
    {feedTreeData.map((node) => (
      <TreeNode
        key={node.id}
        node={node}
        depth={0}
        selectedIds={activeFeedGroup ? new Set([activeFeedGroup]) : new Set()}
        selectedNoteIds={selectedNotes}
        showNotesAsChildren={shouldNestNotesInNavigation}
        edgeSnap={null}
        expanded={expanded}
        feedMode
        onSelect={(event, id) => { event.stopPropagation(); selectFeedGroup(id); }}
        onToggle={handleToggle}
        onNoteSelect={handleNoteSelect}
        onNoteContextMenu={handleNoteContextMenu}
        notePreviews={allNotePreviews}
        onContextMenu={(event, id) => { event.preventDefault(); event.stopPropagation(); selectFeedGroup(id); }}
        indentationWidth={18}
        draggable={false}
      />
    ))}
  </div>
</div>
```
Notice: `feedMode` (boolean prop, truthy shorthand) and `draggable={false}` are the two flags that switch `TreeNode`/`TreeRow`/`NavNoteRow` into "feed" behavior. `edgeSnap={null}` always (edge-snap drop indicators are folder-tree-only).

---

### 2. `model/feed-tree-model.ts` — how pseudo-folders are computed

Full file read (749 lines). Core algorithm:

- `buildFeedTree(notes, previews, hideArchivedNotes)` (line 607) is the entry point. For each note it resolves a timestamp via `getFeedTimestamp` (line 457: `preview?.createdMs ?? preview?.updatedMs ?? null`). Notes with no timestamp (or invalid date) go under a synthetic **"Undated"** bucket (`getUndatedNode`, line 299).
- `addRecentNote` (line 460) buckets by age relative to "now":
  - `ageDays <= 0` → **"Today"** (`kind: "special"`, rank 0)
  - `ageDays === 1` → **"Yesterday"** (rank 1)
  - `ageDays < 7` → **"Last week"** (rank 2), with day-of-week sub-buckets (`kind: "day"`) sorted by `getWeekdayOrder` (Mon-first ordering, line 64)
  - same calendar year, older than a week → `Month` bucket (`kind: "month"`) directly under root, itself containing `Week N` (`kind: "week"`) and weekday `Day` sub-buckets (built via `ensureMonthCalendar`, which pre-populates the *entire* visible calendar skeleton for that month once per month, not per-note — comment at line 348-355 explains this perf optimization)
  - previous years → `Year` → `Quarter` (`Q1`..`Q4`) → `Month` → `Week` → `Day` (lines 561-604)
- Sort order: `SPECIAL_GROUP_ORDER` (line 57: today=0, yesterday=1, last-week=2, undated=99999) plus rank helpers `getMonthSortRank`, `getYearSortRank`, `getQuarterSortRank` that invert calendar order so newest sorts first; `finalizeBuilder` (line 424) sorts children by `rank`, then `latestMs` desc, then name (via a shared `Intl.Collator`, cached — comment lines 48-51 note this is a hot path for perf with thousands of notes).
- `FeedTreeNode` shape (lines 15-27): `id, name, kind ("special"|"year"|"quarter"|"month"|"week"|"day"|"undated"), parentId, rangeStartMs, rangeEndMs, children, notes, noteCount, latestMs, rank`.
- IDs are deterministic path strings built by `buildPathSegments` (line 296), e.g. `feed:month:2026:6`, `feed:year:2025:quarter:2:month:5:week:1:day:12`, `feed:today`, `feed:undated`.
- `buildVisibleFeedNavigationItems` (line 658) flattens the tree into a linear list of `{type: "folder"|"note", id, parentId}` respecting `expanded` set and `shouldNestNotesInNavigation` — this flat list is what `use-feed-keyboard-navigation.ts` walks for Arrow key movement.
- Helpers: `collectFeedNotes`, `getFirstFeedGroupId`, `findFeedNode`, `getLatestFeedTargetTimestamp`.

This is explicitly commented as **not** the real folder tree: "Feed is not the folder tree. It is a synthetic hierarchy built from note timestamps..." (lines 4-5). Real folders live in `model/notes-tree-model.ts` and are backed by actual filesystem folders, not date math.

---

### 3. Row rendering: hover / selected / shift-click

Both Feed buckets and real folders render through `ui/tree-node.tsx` → `ui/tree-row.tsx` (folders/buckets) or `ui/nav-note-row.tsx` (notes) *when not embedded*. But as noted above, the live "Folders" tab actually uses `ui/sidebar-file-tree-node.tsx` (Tailwind shadcn Sidebar), so the *actual on-screen* comparison is `feed-navigation-tree .item-row` (plain CSS) vs shadcn `SidebarMenuButton`/`SidebarMenuSubButton` (Tailwind).

**`ui/tree-row.tsx` markup** (feed bucket rows), lines 86-110:
```
<div
  ref={setRefs}
  style={style}
  className={`item-row folder-row${feedMode ? " feed-bucket-row" : ""}${
    isSelected ? " selected" : ""
  }${
    isDragging ? " is-dragging" : ""
  }${isOver && !edgePosition ? " drop-inside" : ""}${
    edgePosition === "before" ? " drop-before" : ""
  }${edgePosition === "after" ? " drop-after" : ""}`}
  data-folder={node.id}
  onClick={(event) => {
    const target = event.target as HTMLElement | null;
    if (target && target.closest(".tree-toggle, .rename-input")) return;
    onSelect(event, node.id);
  }}
  onContextMenu={(event) => onContextMenu(event, node.id)}
  {...listeners}
  {...attributes}
>
```
So for Feed a row's class string is exactly `item-row folder-row feed-bucket-row` (+ ` selected` when active). The glyph swaps to a `<CalendarDays size={15} />` (lucide-react) instead of folder SVGs when `feedMode` (lines 143-144).

**`ui/nav-note-row.tsx` markup** (note rows under a bucket), line 66-68:
```
className={`item-row nav-note-row${isSelected ? " selected" : ""}${
  isOver ? " drop-inside" : ""
}${isDragging ? " is-dragging" : ""}`}
```

**CSS producing the "full width" hover** — `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/app/app.css`:

Base row rules (shared, lines 433-476):
```css
.item-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 6px;
  padding: 4px 10px;
  padding-right: 72px;
  cursor: pointer;
  user-select: none;
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
  touch-action: none;
}
.item-row.selected { background: var(--ui-select); }
```

Overridden inside `.tree-pane` (lines 616-633):
```css
.tree-pane .item-row {
  border-radius: 0;
  margin: 0;
  min-height: 30px;
  padding: 6px 10px;
  padding-right: 12px;
  transition: background 0.1s ease;
  border: none;
}
.tree-pane .item-row:hover { background: #f7f9fb; }
.tree-pane .item-row.selected {
  background: #f4f8ff;
  box-shadow: inset 2px 0 0 var(--ui-accent);
}
```

Feed-specific override, narrowed by the `feed-navigation-tree` wrapper class from `feed-panel.tsx` (lines 805-820, light theme):
```css
.tree-pane .feed-navigation-tree .item-row {
  width: 100%;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  gap: 8px;
}
.tree-pane .feed-navigation-tree .item-row:hover {
  background: var(--sidebar-accent);
  color: var(--sidebar-accent-foreground);
}
.tree-pane .feed-navigation-tree .item-row.selected {
  background: var(--sidebar-accent);
  color: var(--sidebar-accent-foreground);
  box-shadow: inset 2px 0 0 color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 38%, transparent);
}
```
`--sidebar-accent: oklch(0.967 0.001 286.375)` / `--sidebar-accent-foreground: oklch(0.21 0.006 285.885)` (defined at lines 52-53).

**Why the hover reads as "full width, no inset":** there is *no* horizontal padding anywhere in the ancestor chain for the Feed panel — `.pane` (line 195), `.tree-pane` (534), `.tree-pane .pane-body` (546, `padding: 0 0 10px`), `.nav-scroll-area` (551, no horizontal padding), `.folders-tab-content` (609, layout-only) — and `.item-row` itself has `width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box` for Feed rows specifically. So the hover/selected background paints edge-to-edge against the sidebar's outer border, with square corners (no `border-radius`, explicitly `border-radius: 0` at line 617).

This is unlike the *real* Folders tab (embedded shadcn Sidebar), where `.sidebar-folders-section .nav-scroll-area { padding: 0 8px 10px; }` (line 300) insets the whole list 8px from each edge, and `SidebarMenuButton`'s Tailwind classes include `rounded-md` (`sidebarMenuButtonVariants`, `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/shared/ui/sidebar.tsx:475`) — so Folders' hover/active pill is inset and rounded, not full-bleed.

**Dark theme caveat (specificity bug/quirk worth knowing):** dark-mode overrides at lines 2579-2590:
```css
.app.theme-dark .tree-pane .item-row { color: #dce2ea; }
.app.theme-dark .tree-pane .item-row:hover { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045); }
.app.theme-dark .tree-pane .item-row.selected {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  box-shadow: inset 2px 0 0 rgba(210, 210, 216, 0.58);
}
```
These selectors have **higher specificity** (5 simple selectors: `.app.theme-dark.tree-pane.item-row:hover`) than the feed-scoped rules (`.tree-pane .feed-navigation-tree .item-row:hover`, 4 simple selectors), so in dark mode the Feed hover/selected background actually falls back to the generic dark-mode color (`rgba(255,255,255,0.045)` / `rgba(255,255,255,0.12)`) rather than `var(--sidebar-accent)` — the `--sidebar-accent` styling for Feed is effectively light-mode-only in practice.

**Shift-click multi-select** (shared across Feed and Folders) — `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/shared/lib/selection.ts`, `computeRangeSelection` (lines 18-44):
```ts
export function computeRangeSelection(
  event: SelectionModifiers,
  current: Set<string>,
  order: string[],
  lastSelected: string | null,
  path: string
): Set<string> {
  const next = new Set(current);
  if (event.shiftKey && lastSelected) {
    next.clear();
    const start = order.indexOf(lastSelected);
    const end = order.indexOf(path);
    if (start !== -1 && end !== -1) {
      const [from, to] = start < end ? [start, end] : [end, start];
      order.slice(from, to + 1).forEach((id) => next.add(id));
    } else {
      next.add(path);
    }
  } else if (event.metaKey || event.ctrlKey) {
    if (next.has(path)) next.delete(path);
    else next.add(path);
  } else {
    next.clear();
    next.add(path);
  }
  return next;
}
```
Feed calls this from `handleNoteSelect` (`feed-panel.tsx:93-126`) with `order = parentNode?.notes.map(n => n.path)` — i.e. the range is scoped to *notes within the clicked note's own date bucket only* (shift-click cannot span across two different day/week/month buckets). This mirrors, but is a separate call site from, the generic `handleNoteClick` in `use-tree-interactions.ts` (lines 171-191) used for the real folder tree, which scopes the range to `parentNode.notes` of the real folder instead. Feed does **not** import/use `useTreeInteractions` at all — it only imports its `DesktopContextMenuState` type (line 8 of `feed-panel.tsx`) and reimplements its own click handlers locally.

---

### 4. Tailwind/font classes for Feed rows (for comparison against Folders)

Feed uses **plain custom CSS classes**, not Tailwind utilities, for its row typography:

- Bucket label: `<span className="item-label">{node.name}</span>` (`tree-row.tsx:196`) → styled by `.tree-pane .item-label` (app.css:717-722): `font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0; color: var(--ui-text);`
- Note label under a bucket: `<span className="item-label">{title}</span>` (`nav-note-row.tsx:106`) → additionally narrowed by `.tree-pane .nav-note-row .item-label` (app.css:643-646): `font-size: 13px; font-weight: 450;`
- Note count badge: `<span className="note-count">` → `.tree-pane .note-count` (724-736): `font-size: 12px; color: var(--ui-muted); opacity: .78; font-weight: 500;`
- Row min-height for feed buckets specifically: `.tree-pane .feed-navigation-tree .feed-bucket-row { min-height: 32px; padding-top: 5px; padding-bottom: 5px; }` (831-835), vs generic `.tree-pane .item-row { min-height: 30px; }` (619) and `.tree-pane .nav-note-row { min-height: 28px; }` (639-641).
- `font-family` is never set on these classes — they inherit from `.tree-pane { font-family: inherit; }` (line 537), which cascades from the app root font.

By contrast, **Folders rows** (as actually rendered, via `SidebarMenuButton`) get their type styling from Tailwind utility strings baked into `sidebarMenuButtonVariants` in `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/shared/ui/sidebar.tsx:474-494`:
```
"peer/menu-button flex w-full items-center gap-2 overflow-hidden rounded-md p-2 text-left text-sm outline-hidden ... hover:bg-sidebar-accent hover:text-sidebar-accent-foreground ... data-[active=true]:bg-sidebar-accent data-[active=true]:font-medium data-[active=true]:text-sidebar-accent-foreground ..."
size variants: default: "h-8 text-sm", sm: "h-7 text-xs", lg: "h-12 text-sm ..."
```
and `SidebarMenuSubButton` (note rows) at `sidebar.tsx:687-690`:
```
"text-sidebar-foreground ... hover:bg-sidebar-accent hover:text-sidebar-accent-foreground ... flex h-7 min-w-0 -translate-x-px items-center gap-2 overflow-hidden rounded-md px-2 ..."
size === "sm" && "text-xs"
size === "md" && "text-sm"
```
So: Folders' bucket/folder row text is Tailwind `text-sm` (14px default), and it becomes `font-medium` (500 weight) only `data-[active=true]` (i.e. only when selected — not always 500 like Feed's `.item-label`). Folders' note rows (`SidebarMenuSubButton` with `size="md"` per `sidebar-file-tree-node.tsx:141-143`) are Tailwind `text-sm` (14px) — **not** `text-xs`/13px like Feed's `.nav-note-row .item-label` (13px/450). So Feed's note rows currently render one step smaller/lighter than Folders' note rows — that's the concrete font delta to check.

---

### 5. Drag-and-drop / reordering — confirmed absent for Feed

- `feed-panel.tsx:235`: `draggable={false}` is passed into the top-level `TreeNode` for every feed bucket, and `tree-node.tsx` propagates `draggable` unchanged to every recursive child `TreeNode` (line 136) and to `NavNoteRow` (line 110).
- `tree-row.tsx:59-68`: `useDraggable({ ..., disabled: !draggable })` and `useDroppable({ ..., disabled: !draggable })` — with `draggable=false`, dnd-kit disables both the drag source and the drop target for feed bucket rows.
- `nav-note-row.tsx:38-47`: identical `disabled: !draggable` pattern for feed note rows.
- Even though `{...listeners} {...attributes}` are still spread onto the DOM node (tree-row.tsx:108-109, nav-note-row.tsx:72-73), dnd-kit's `useDraggable` returns no-op listeners when `disabled` is true, so no pointer/drag events are actually wired up.
- Structurally, the entire reordering engine (`hooks/use-drag-drop.ts`, `model/tree-dnd.ts`, `moveItems`/`setOrder` API calls) operates only on the real folder `treeData`/`tree` (filesystem folders) — it has no concept of feed buckets at all, and `feed-panel.tsx` never passes `feedTreeData` into any of that machinery. `edgeSnap={null}` is hardcoded in the Feed render (line 218), so the before/after drop-line indicators (`drop-before`/`drop-after` CSS, app.css:454-470, 698-703) can never appear for Feed rows either.

Conclusion: Feed rows are fully inert with respect to drag/reorder, both at the prop level (`draggable={false}` disabling dnd-kit hooks) and at the business-logic level (the DnD reducer only knows about the real folder tree).

---

### 6. Shared hooks Feed uses for click/select/expand-collapse

Feed does **not** use `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/app/hooks/use-tree-interactions.ts` (`useTreeInteractions`) — that hook is wired up only for the real Folders tree in `desktop-app-shell.tsx` (`handleFolderClick`, `handleToggle`, `handleNoteClick`, `handleFolderContextMenu`, `handleNoteContextMenu` all come from `useTreeInteractions` and are passed to `<FoldersPanel>`). It's imported into `feed-panel.tsx` only for its `DesktopContextMenuState` **type** (line 8), so the two context-menu shapes stay compatible.

Feed instead has its own bespoke, parallel implementations:
- Local `selectFeedGroup`, `handleNoteSelect`, `handleToggle`, `handleNoteContextMenu` defined directly inside `feed-panel.tsx` (lines 64-184) — functionally analogous to `useTreeInteractions`'s `handleFolderClick`/`handleNoteClick`/`handleToggle`/`handleFolderContextMenu`/`handleNoteContextMenu`, but scoped to feed buckets/`activeFeedGroup` instead of folders/`activeFolder`.
- `hooks/use-feed-keyboard-navigation.ts` (`useFeedKeyboardNavigation`) — the Feed-only analog of the (separate) `hooks/use-keyboard-navigation.ts` used for the real folder tree. It walks `feedVisibleNavigationItems` (built by `buildVisibleFeedNavigationItems` in `feed-tree-model.ts:658`) for Arrow Up/Down/Left/Right, calling local `selectFeedGroup`/`selectFeedNote` closures (lines 77-111) that mirror the same "clear note selection, set `FEED_FOLDER_PATH`, focus + scroll into view via `data-folder`/`data-note` attribute selectors" pattern as the click handlers.
- Both Feed and Folders bottom out on the same low-level primitives: `computeRangeSelection`/`resolveTargetPaths` (`shared/lib/selection.ts`) and `focusNoScroll`/`scrollIntoViewIfNeeded`/`escapeSelectorValue` (`/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/shared/lib/dom.ts`) — those are the only genuinely shared behavior primitives; the higher-level orchestration is duplicated per-surface rather than reused via `useTreeInteractions`.
